<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abide with Me</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1847">1847</a> (an account of <a href="/years/1925">1925</a> dates it to <a href="/years/1820">1820</a>)</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Abide with Me&quot; is a Christian hymn by the Anglican cleric Henry Francis Lyte (1793–1847). Lyte was a curate in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-wexford">County Wexford</a> from 1815 to 1818, where he often preached at the church in Killurin and came under the lasting influence of its rector, the Reverend Abraham Swanne; he was later vicar of All Saints' Church in Brixham, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/devon">Devon</a>.</p></div>
